# Operators (emitter.warp's part): arithmetic and comparisons on numbers and on boxed values, equality, ø tests
# `30° * 2`: arithmetic keeps a marked operand's mark (decision marks-survive-arithmetic), the left one's, else the
# right one's, where it marks a number of the result's kind; a boxed operand's by the runtime's marks_kept
def operation_code(body: Body, symbol: text, a: TypedCode, b: TypedCode): TypedCode {
	marked(symbol, unmarked_operation(body, symbol, a, b), a, b)
}
# an arithmetic result with the mark of its operands: unboxed, carried statically; boxed (an int's grown or exact
# result), stamped by the runtime's kept_mark
def marked(symbol: text, result: TypedCode, a: TypedCode, b: TypedCode): TypedCode {
	if symbol in comparisons or (a.mark == 0 and b.mark == 0) or result.mark != 0 { return result }
	if result.kind == ValueKind.Node and module.runtime.has("kept_mark") { return runtime_call("kept_mark", [result, number_value(if a.mark != 0 then a.mark else b.mark)]) }
	mark = if marks_kind(a.mark, result.kind) then a.mark else if marks_kind(b.mark, result.kind) then b.mark else 0
	if mark != 0 { return TypedCode(result.kind, result.code, mark) }
	result
}
marks_kind(mark: int, kind: ValueKind): bool := mark != 0 and ((kind == ValueKind.Int and mark % KindUnit.Info == Kind.Int) or (kind == ValueKind.Float and mark % KindUnit.Info == Kind.Float))
def unmarked_operation(body: Body, symbol: text, a: TypedCode, b: TypedCode): TypedCode {
	# an element of a recursive call's result the first reading does not know yet: its index says nothing of its kind
	if symbol == "#" and a.kind == pending { return element(body, TypedCode(ValueKind.Node, a.code), b) }
	# a recursive call's result the first reading does not know yet is of the other operand's kind: `[n] + f(n - 1)`
	if a.kind == pending and b.kind != pending { a = TypedCode(b.kind, a.code) }
	if b.kind == pending and a.kind != pending { b = TypedCode(a.kind, b.code) }
	kind = joint_kind(a.kind, b.kind)
	# two results not known yet: computed as ints, but of a kind still pending, so `f(x) + g(x) + [y]` reads again
	unknown = kind == pending
	if unknown { kind = ValueKind.Int }
	if symbol == "#" and (a.kind == ValueKind.List or a.kind == ValueKind.Node) { return element(body, a, b) }
	if symbol == "#" and a.kind == ValueKind.Text { return runtime_call("text_char", [a, whole_index(b)]) }
	if symbol == "+" and a.kind == ValueKind.List and b.kind == ValueKind.List { return runtime_call("list_join", [a, b]) }
	# a list takes any other value as its last item: `[1] + "a"` is [1 'a'] (runtime arithmetic.warp node_add)
	if symbol == "+" and a.kind == ValueKind.List and b.kind != ValueKind.Node { return runtime_call("list_join", [a, TypedCode(ValueKind.List, vector_code([boxed(b)]))]) }
	textual = is_textual(a.kind) or is_textual(b.kind)
	if symbol == "+" and textual { return runtime_call("text_join", [shown_text(a), shown_text(b)]) }
	# `d + 1 day`, `a - b` of a time: lib/time_arithmetic.warp's time_operation
	if (a.kind == ValueKind.Time or b.kind == ValueKind.Time) and symbol in time_operators and module.functions.has(time_operation_word) { return time_operation_call(body, symbol, a, b) }
	structured = a.kind == ValueKind.List or b.kind == ValueKind.List or a.kind == ValueKind.Node or b.kind == ValueKind.Node
	# a boxed operand may be an instance whose class defines the operator: its dispatcher (class_methods.warp's
	# `+·operator`, the operator a codepoint) calls the method, the right operand's for a commutative one (`5 * q`), or
	# on any other values this builtin, which its own body keeps
	dispatcher = "${symbol}·operator"
	if (a.kind == ValueKind.Node or b.kind == ValueKind.Node) and dispatcher in module.functions and body.function.name != dispatcher { return call_values(module.functions[dispatcher], [TypedCode(ValueKind.Node, boxed(a)), TypedCode(ValueKind.Node, boxed(b))]) }
	if structured and symbol in equalities { return equality(body, symbol, a, b) }
	# `"ab" * 2.5`: Rust says how a text repeats, a trap could not
	if textual and (a.kind == ValueKind.Node or b.kind == ValueKind.Node) and symbol not in comparisons { return refuse("the operator " + symbol + " on " + kind_spelling(a.kind) + " and " + kind_spelling(b.kind)) }
	if a.kind == ValueKind.Node or b.kind == ValueKind.Node { return node_operation(body, symbol, boxed(a), boxed(b)) }
	# `"ab" * 3`, `3 * " "`: the text repeated, as `3 times "ab"`
	if symbol == "*" and is_textual(a.kind) and b.kind == ValueKind.Int { return runtime_call("repeated_text", [b, TypedCode(ValueKind.Node, boxed(a))]) }
	if symbol == "*" and is_textual(b.kind) and a.kind == ValueKind.Int { return runtime_call("repeated_text", [a, TypedCode(ValueKind.Node, boxed(b))]) }
	if symbol in comparisons and a.kind == ValueKind.Char and b.kind == ValueKind.Char { return operation_code(body, symbol, code_point(a), code_point(b)) }
	if symbol in comparisons and textual and is_textual(a.kind) and is_textual(b.kind) {
		return operation_code(body, symbol, runtime_call("text_order", [shown_text(a), shown_text(b)]), number_value(0))
	}
	# `a < b` of two dates, `1 month > 27 days`: equal as nodes, ordered by time_holds (runtime/extended/times.warp)
	if a.kind == ValueKind.Time and b.kind == ValueKind.Time and symbol in equalities { return equality(body, symbol, TypedCode(ValueKind.Node, a.code), TypedCode(ValueKind.Node, b.code)) }
	if a.kind == ValueKind.Time and b.kind == ValueKind.Time and symbol in time_relations { return runtime_call("time_holds", [a, b, number_value(time_relations[symbol])]) }
	if kind == ValueKind.Bool and symbol in bool_ops { return TypedCode(ValueKind.Bool, a.code + b.code + [bool_ops[symbol]]) }
	if kind != ValueKind.Int and kind != ValueKind.Float { return refuse("the operator " + symbol + " on " + kind_spelling(a.kind) + " and " + kind_spelling(b.kind)) }
	if symbol == "%" and kind == ValueKind.Int { return euclidean_remainder(body, a, b) }
	if symbol == "%" { return runtime_call("float_mod", [TypedCode(ValueKind.Float, converted(a, kind)), TypedCode(ValueKind.Float, converted(b, kind))]) }
	if symbol == "rem" and kind == ValueKind.Float { return float_remainder(body, converted(a, kind), converted(b, kind)) }
	if symbol == "/" and kind == ValueKind.Int { return runtime_call("exact_ratio", [a, b]) }
	# a negative exponent gives an exact rational, so the power is a boxed value
	if symbol == "^" and kind == ValueKind.Int { return runtime_call("exact_pow", [TypedCode(ValueKind.Node, boxed(a)), TypedCode(ValueKind.Node, boxed(b))]) }
	if symbol == "^" { return float_power(body, converted(a, kind), converted(b, kind)) }
	ops = if kind == ValueKind.Float then float_ops else int_ops
	if symbol not in ops { return refuse("the operator " + symbol + " on " + kind_spelling(kind)) }
	result = if symbol in comparisons then ValueKind.Bool else if unknown then pending else kind
	TypedCode(result, converted(a, kind) + converted(b, kind) + [ops[symbol]])
}

# base ^ exponent of floats: the runtime word float_pow (runtime/extended/pow.warp, musl's pow); a NaN (a negative base to a fraction) fails as invalid_number, as in Rust
def float_power(body: Body, base: list, exponent: list): TypedCode {
	held = uleb(fresh_local(body, ValueKind.Float))
	code = runtime_call("float_pow", [TypedCode(ValueKind.Float, base), TypedCode(ValueKind.Float, exponent)]).code + [op.local_tee] + held + [op.local_get] + held
	checked = [op.f64_ne, op.if, no_value] + dropped(runtime_call("invalid_number", [])) + [op.end]
	TypedCode(ValueKind.Float, code + checked + [op.local_get] + held)
}

# an operator on boxed values, by the kinds they hold at run time: `+` is the runtime word node_add; a comparison
# between two texts or characters orders them as texts; two ints stay ints; an exact rational with an int or another
# stays exact; any other two are floats
def node_operation(body: Body, symbol: text, a: list, b: list): TypedCode {
	if symbol == "+" { return runtime_call("node_add", [TypedCode(ValueKind.Node, a), TypedCode(ValueKind.Node, b)]) }
	# a bit operator takes ints only: `1 << place` of a value known only at run time reads it as an int
	if symbol in bit_operators { return operation_code(body, symbol, TypedCode(ValueKind.Int, converted(TypedCode(ValueKind.Node, a), ValueKind.Int)), TypedCode(ValueKind.Int, converted(TypedCode(ValueKind.Node, b), ValueKind.Int))) }
	left = TypedCode(ValueKind.Node, [op.local_get] + uleb(fresh_local(body, ValueKind.Node)))
	right = TypedCode(ValueKind.Node, [op.local_get] + uleb(fresh_local(body, ValueKind.Node)))
	plain = [TypedCode(ValueKind.Int, unboxed(left.code, gc_type(gc.int_box))), TypedCode(ValueKind.Int, unboxed(right.code, gc_type(gc.int_box)))]
	# two plain ints past 64 bits make a big int (D16): the runtime's grown words
	ints = if symbol in grown_words then runtime_call(grown_words[symbol], plain) else operation_code(body, symbol, plain#1, plain#2)
	floats = operation_code(body, symbol, runtime_call("float_of_node", [left]), runtime_call("float_of_node", [right]))
	kind = if ints.kind == ValueKind.Bool then ValueKind.Bool else ValueKind.Node
	exact = exact_operation(body, symbol, left, right, floats)
	# two Ints in $i64boxes stay ints; a ratio or a big int on either side takes the exact word
	integers = plain_int_test(left.code) + plain_int_test(right.code) + [op.i32_and] + if_else_code(kind, ints, exact)
	numbers = both_of_kind(left.code, right.code, Kind.Int) + if_else_code(kind, TypedCode(kind, integers), floats)
	code = a + [op.local_set] + left.code[1..] + b + [op.local_set] + right.code[1..]
	# (a runtime built before marks_kept, the seed's, keeps none)
	if symbol not in comparisons and module.runtime.has("marks_kept") { return runtime_call("marks_kept", [TypedCode(kind, code + numbers), left, right]) }
	if symbol not in comparisons { return TypedCode(kind, code + numbers) }
	texts = operation_code(body, symbol, runtime_call("node_text", [left]), runtime_call("node_text", [right]))
	textual = x => condition(runtime_call("textual_node", [x]))
	TypedCode(kind, code + textual(left) + textual(right) + [op.i32_and] + if_else_code(kind, texts, TypedCode(kind, numbers)))
}
# `x == ø`, `x === ø` and their negations (a match's `ø:` case): x is ø itself, missing; an empty list, text or map
# is a value (decision empty-is-not-missing)
def identity_with_nothing(body: Body, symbol: text, n: Node): TypedCode {
	tested_as(symbol, TypedCode(ValueKind.Bool, boxed(expression_code(body, n)) + [op.ref_is_null]))
}
# `a == b`, `a != b` with a list or a boxed value: the runtime word node_equal compares them deeply
def equality(body: Body, symbol: text, a: TypedCode, b: TypedCode): TypedCode {
	tested_as(symbol, runtime_call("node_equal", [TypedCode(ValueKind.Node, boxed(a)), TypedCode(ValueKind.Node, boxed(b))]))
}
# the bool test as `==`, `===` ask it, negated for `!=`, `!==`
def tested_as(symbol: text, test: TypedCode): TypedCode := if symbol.starts_with("!") then TypedCode(ValueKind.Bool, condition(test) + [op.i32_eqz]) else test
# an operator on two Int $Nodes, one an exact rational: the runtime's exact word, a comparison by exact_order; the
# operators without one take the floats
grown_words = {"+": "grown_sum", "-": "grown_difference", "*": "grown_product"}
# `a + b`, `a - b`, `a * b` of two ints (decision nat-and-int): a whole number may grow past 64 bits, so the grown
# words give it boxed, a big int past i64; two fast ints wrap as wasm's i64, as do the runtime's own words
def arithmetic(body: Body, symbol: text, left: Node, right: Node): TypedCode {
	a = expression_code(body, left)
	b = expression_code(body, right)
	if symbol in grown_words and wraps(body, left, right) {
		a = unboxed_int_slot(body, left, a)
		b = unboxed_int_slot(body, right, b)
	}
	if symbol in grown_words and a.kind == ValueKind.Int and b.kind == ValueKind.Int and not wraps(body, left, right) { return marked(symbol, runtime_call(grown_words[symbol], [a, b]), a, b) }
	operation_code(body, symbol, a, b)
}
# a variable declared int in an optional or union slot holds a node, an int still (boxing is the layout, not the type)
boxed_int_slot(body: Body, n: Node): bool := n is symbol and name_of(n) in body.boxed_ints
unboxed_int_slot(body: Body, n: Node, value: TypedCode): TypedCode := if value.kind == ValueKind.Node and boxed_int_slot(body, n) then TypedCode(ValueKind.Int, converted(value, ValueKind.Int)) else value
# a literal beside a fast int takes the int side: `i + 1` of a counter wraps
wraps(body: Body, left: Node, right: Node): bool := body.function.is_runtime or (fast_int(body, left) and fast_int(body, right)) or (left is number and fast_int(body, right)) or (right is number and fast_int(body, left))
# a fast int: a variable or parameter declared int (a loop's counter is), a call of a function declared int, `#xs`, + - * of fast ints
fast_int(body: Body, n: Node): bool := {
	if n is symbol { return declared_int(body, name_of(n)) }
	if is_key(n, Op.Hash) and key_of(n) == ø { return yes }
	if is_round(n) and #n > 0 and n#1 is symbol and name_of(n#1) in module.functions { return gives_declared_int(module.functions[name_of(n#1)]) }
	type(n) is key and op_of(n) in grown_words and key_of(n) != ø and wraps(body, key_of(n), value_of(n))
}
# a call of a function declared to give an int, `f(): int := 3` (decision declared-int-result)
gives_declared_int(f: Function): bool := declared_kinds.get(aliased_type(declared_result_word(f) ?? "")) == ValueKind.Int
declared_int(body: Body, name: text): bool := (name in body.declared and body.declared[name] == ValueKind.Int) or name in body.boxed_ints or body.function.signature.parameters.any(p => p.name == name and p.type_name and declared_kinds.get(aliased_type(p.type_name)) == ValueKind.Int)
exact_words = {"-": "exact_sub", "*": "exact_mul", "/": "exact_div", "%": "exact_mod", "rem": "exact_rem"}
def exact_operation(body: Body, symbol: text, left: TypedCode, right: TypedCode, floats: TypedCode): TypedCode {
	if symbol in exact_words { return runtime_call(exact_words[symbol], [left, right]) }
	if symbol in comparisons { return operation_code(body, symbol, runtime_call("exact_order", [left, right]), number_value(0)) }
	floats
}
# `floor x`: an int itself, a float's floor as an int, a boxed number by the runtime word floored_node (exact for a
# ratio, as Rust's exact_floor)
# `type(x)`: the type value of x's kind, of a value known only at run time the one its kind names there (a list's
# items unknown here, Rust's `list of int`, outside the core)
static_type_word(kind: ValueKind): text? := match kind {
	ValueKind.Int: "int"
	ValueKind.Float: "float"
	ValueKind.Text: "text"
	ValueKind.Char: "codepoint"
	ValueKind.Bool: "bool"
	_: ø
}
# a whole number is a nat but where it is a fast int, declared int (decision nat-and-int)
def type_value_of(body: Body, n: Node): TypedCode {
	value = expression_code(body, n)
	if value.kind == ValueKind.Node and boxed_int_slot(body, n) { return runtime_call("int_slot_type_name", [value, list_value(body, module.classes.keys)]) }
	if value.kind == ValueKind.Node { return runtime_call("node_type_name", [value, list_value(body, module.classes.keys)]) }
	word = if value.kind == ValueKind.Int and not fast_int(body, n) then "nat" else static_type_word(value.kind)
	if word != ø { return TypedCode(ValueKind.Node, node(Marked.TypeValue, text_bytes(word))) }
	refuse("the type of a " + kind_spelling(value.kind))
}
# ord(c): the code point of a character, of a text its first; chr(n) the character of the code point n
def code_point(value: TypedCode): TypedCode {
	if value.kind == ValueKind.Text { return runtime_call("code_point_at", [value, TypedCode(ValueKind.Int, [op.i64_const] + sleb(0))]) }
	TypedCode(ValueKind.Int, converted(value, ValueKind.Char) + [op.i64_extend_i32_u])
}
# float_bits(x): the IEEE 754 bits of a float as an int; bits_float(n): the float of those bits
bit_casts = {float_bits: [ValueKind.Float, ValueKind.Int, "i64.reinterpret_f64"], bits_float: [ValueKind.Int, ValueKind.Float, "f64.reinterpret_i64"]}
def bit_cast(value: TypedCode, cast: list): TypedCode { TypedCode(cast#2, converted(value, cast#1) + [wasm_instructions[cast#3]]) }
def floored(value: TypedCode): TypedCode {
	if value.kind == ValueKind.Int { return value }
	if value.kind == ValueKind.Float { return TypedCode(ValueKind.Int, value.code + [op.f64_floor, op.i64_trunc_f64_s]) }
	if value.kind == ValueKind.Node or value.kind == pending { return runtime_call("floored_node", [TypedCode(ValueKind.Node, value.code)]) }
	refuse("floor of a " + kind_spelling(value.kind))
}
# `if` on the condition just computed: yes gives a, no gives b, both as kind
def if_else_code(kind: ValueKind, a: TypedCode, b: TypedCode): list { [op.if] + value_type(kind) + converted(a, kind) + [op.else] + converted(b, kind) + [op.end] }
def both_of_kind(a: list, b: list, code: int): list {
	test = x => kind_code_of(x) + [op.i64_const] + sleb(code) + [op.i64_eq]
	test(a) + test(b) + [op.i32_and]
}

# `‖x‖`, abs(x): -x when x < 0, else x
def absolute_value(body: Body, value: TypedCode): TypedCode {
	if value.kind == ValueKind.Float { return TypedCode(ValueKind.Float, value.code + [op.f64_abs]) }
	if value.kind != ValueKind.Int and value.kind != ValueKind.Node { return refuse("the absolute value of a " + kind_spelling(value.kind)) }
	local = uleb(fresh_local(body, value.kind))
	saved = TypedCode(value.kind, [op.local_get] + local)
	below_zero = condition(operation_code(body, "<", saved, number_value(0)))
	TypedCode(value.kind, value.code + [op.local_set] + local + below_zero + [op.if] + value_type(value.kind) + negation(body, saved).code + [op.else] + saved.code + [op.end])
}

# a % b as in mathematics: never below 0, r + |b| for a negative truncated remainder r; b = 0 fails in divide_by_zero,
# which names the error (the engine's own trap knows no source position)
def euclidean_remainder(body: Body, a: TypedCode, b: TypedCode): TypedCode {
	divisor = uleb(fresh_local(body, ValueKind.Int))
	rest = uleb(fresh_local(body, ValueKind.Int))
	get_divisor = [op.local_get] + divisor
	get_rest = [op.local_get] + rest
	zero = [op.i64_const, 0]
	absolute = zero + get_divisor + [op.i64_sub] + get_divisor + get_divisor + zero + [op.i64_lt_s, op.select]
	nonzero = [op.local_tee] + divisor + [op.i64_eqz, op.if, no_value] + runtime_call("divide_by_zero", []).code + [op.drop, op.end] + get_divisor
	code = a.code + b.code + nonzero + [op.i64_rem_s, op.local_set] + rest + get_rest + zero + [op.i64_lt_s]
	TypedCode(ValueKind.Int, code + [op.if, type_bytes.int] + get_rest + absolute + [op.i64_add, op.else] + get_rest + [op.end])
}
